# https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Acroteria
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Acroteria> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Acroteria> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalElement> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Acroteria> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Acroteria"@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Acroteria> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "An ornament placed at the summit or at a lower corner of a pediment. Each ornament can be recorded individually, whether it takes the form of foliage, a figure or another sculptural motif."@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Acroteria> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/hasAATReference> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300002214> .
# 
# https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Aedicules
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Aedicules> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Aedicules> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalAssemblies> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Aedicules> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Aedicules"@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Aedicules> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "A small shrine or architectural frame that gives a niche, image or opening the form of a miniature building. Supports and a crowning member define the frame."@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Aedicules> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/hasAATReference> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300002574> .
# 
# https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Arch
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Arch> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Arch> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalElement> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Arch> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Arch"@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Arch> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "A curved or pointed construction spanning an opening and transmitting load to supports at its springings. Its constituent voussoirs may be recorded individually."@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Arch> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/hasAATReference> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300000994> .
# 
# https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchType
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchType> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E55_Type> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Arch Type"@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchType> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "A controlled concept used to classify an arch by a stated criterion such as profile or construction."@en .
# 
# https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalAssemblies
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalAssemblies> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalAssemblies> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalElement> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalAssemblies> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Architectural Assemblies"@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalAssemblies> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "An arrangement of architectural elements identifiable as a single composition. Its identity depends on how the members work together, even where individual elements also have records."@en .
# 
# https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalDecorationType
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalDecorationType> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalDecorationType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E55_Type> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalDecorationType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Architectural Decoration Type"@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalDecorationType> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "A controlled concept classifying an architectural decorative feature by its form, medium or motif. The same concept may describe decorative features on different supporting elements."@en .
# 
# https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalDecorativeFeature
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalDecorativeFeature> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalDecorativeFeature> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E25_Human-Made_Feature> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalDecorativeFeature> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Architectural Decorative Feature"@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalDecorativeFeature> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "This class comprises identifiable decorative features intentionally created on or within architectural elements through human activity. Such features are physically integrated with their supporting architectural elements and cannot be separated from them without altering their physical integrity.\n\nInstances of this class may include figurative paintings, frescoes, graffiti, carved reliefs, ornamental motifs, decorative moldings, and modeled stucco decorations executed directly on architectural surfaces. These features may serve aesthetic, artistic, symbolic, or iconographic purposes and do not necessarily perform a structural function."@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalDecorativeFeature> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/hasAATReference> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300378995> .
# 
# https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalElement
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalElement> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalElement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E24_Physical_Human-Made_Thing> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalElement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Architectural Element"@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalElement> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "A physically identifiable element of an architectural work, distinguished by its architectural form, function, or constructional characteristics, whether or not it constitutes an independently manufactured or assembled unit."@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalElement> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/hasAATReference> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300000885> .
# 
# https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalSpace
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalSpace> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalSpace> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E53_Place> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalSpace> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Architectural Space"@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalSpace> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "This class comprises identifiable spatial regions within or associated with architectural works, defined by their architectural configuration, spatial boundaries, or architectural functions. Instances of this class may be enclosed, partially enclosed, or open spaces, including rooms, halls, corridors, naves, chapels, and courtyards.\n\nAn architectural space may be defined or bounded by one or more architectural elements, such as walls, columns, floors, and vaults. The spatial extent of an architectural space may overlap with the physical volume occupied by architectural elements, depending on how its boundaries are defined. Architectural spaces may contain physical objects, including furniture, sculptures, and other movable or immovable objects.\n\nInstances of this class may be associated with a building as a whole or with a particular storey. They may also extend across multiple storeys and have spatial relationships with other architectural spaces, such as adjacency and containment."@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalSpace> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/hasAATReference> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300420294> .
# 
# https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalStratigraphicUnit
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalStratigraphicUnit> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalStratigraphicUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E24_Physical_Human-Made_Thing> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalStratigraphicUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Architectural Stratigraphic Unit"@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalStratigraphicUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "This class comprises physically identifiable portions of historic buildings formed through distinguishable episodes of human construction, reconstruction, modification, or repair. Each instance represents a stratigraphically coherent physical unit, which may consist of multiple materials or construction elements, with recognizable boundaries or discontinuities that distinguish it from adjacent building fabric and provide evidence of its formation history.\n\nInstances may remain physically integrated with the surrounding building fabric while retaining a distinct stratigraphic identity. Their identification does not necessarily require a precise date or attribution to a known historical event."@en .
# 
# https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalStyle
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalStyle> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalStyle> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E55_Type> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalStyle> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Architectural Style"@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalStyle> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "This class comprises controlled concepts used to classify buildings, architectural elements, architectural stratigraphic units, constructional layers and discrete building units according to characteristic formal, compositional and decorative features associated with recognised architectural styles or historical traditions. Stylistic categories may be identified through architectural design, proportions, ornamentation and other morphological characteristics. An entity may be associated with multiple architectural styles where construction, modification or restoration reflects different stylistic influences."@en .
# 
# https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Architrave
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Architrave> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Architrave> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalElement> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Architrave> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Architrave"@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Architrave> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "In the context of a classical entablature, the lowermost horizontal division immediately above the supports."@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Architrave> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/hasAATReference> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300001780> .
# 
# https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Ashlar
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Ashlar> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Ashlar> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/DiscreteBuildingUnit> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Ashlar> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Ashlar"@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Ashlar> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "An individual dressed building stone with accurately worked bedding and joint faces. Here the record identifies a block within the masonry."@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Ashlar> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/hasAATReference> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300011701> .
# 
# https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Audio
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Audio> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Audio> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E73_Information_Object> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Audio> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Audio"@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Audio> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "This class comprises identifiable information resources whose content is primarily expressed through sound. It includes audio recordings, oral histories, interviews, spoken narratives, and environmental or architectural sound recordings associated with built heritage. Audio resources may document actual events and existing conditions, communicate historical interpretations, or present proposed experiences and narratives. The class is defined by its auditory form rather than its documentary purpose, linguistic content, recording technology, or digital file format."@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Audio> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/hasAATReference> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300028633> .
# 
# https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/BIMModel
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/BIMModel> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/BIMModel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E73_Information_Object> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/BIMModel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "BIM Model"@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/BIMModel> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "This class comprises identifiable digital building information resources that organize architectural and construction-related information through structured representations of buildings, their components, attributes, and relationships. BIM models may integrate geometric representations with semantic descriptions, material information, spatial organization, and other building-related data. They may describe existing buildings, proposed designs, historical reconstructions, or conservation interventions. The class includes Heritage Building Information Models (HBIM) and is independent of a particular authoring application, exchange format, or geometric representation method. Unlike a purely geometric model, a BIM model provides an explicit information structure for representing building elements and their associated properties and relationships."@en .
# 
# https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Building
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Building> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Building> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E24_Physical_Human-Made_Thing> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Building> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Building"@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Building> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "This class comprises physically constructed buildings that form identifiable architectural wholes, consisting of interconnected architectural elements and enclosing or organising spaces. A building may contain multiple storeys and architectural spaces and retains its identity despite changes in function or internal spatial organisation."@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Building> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/hasAATReference> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300004792> .
# 
# https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/BuildingType
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/BuildingType> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/BuildingType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E55_Type> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/BuildingType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Building Type"@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/BuildingType> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "This class comprises controlled concepts used to classify buildings according to their intended function, historical or current use, or architectural organization. Instances of this class may describe functional or typological categories, and a building may be assigned multiple types or different classifications over time as its use or interpretation changes."@en .
# 
# https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ClassicalOrder
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ClassicalOrder> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ClassicalOrder> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E55_Type> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ClassicalOrder> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Classical Order"@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ClassicalOrder> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "This class comprises controlled concepts representing classical architectural orders used to classify architectural elements according to their formal and stylistic characteristics. The five orders considered are Doric, Ionic, Corinthian, Tuscan, and Composite. These concepts are identified using Getty Art & Architecture Thesaurus (AAT) URIs."@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ClassicalOrder> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/hasAATReference> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404750> .
# 
# https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Column
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Column> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Column> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalElement> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Column> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Column"@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Column> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "An upright architectural member with a shaft, used to carry a load or to express support. The shaft, capital and any base may be identified individually."@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Column> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/hasAATReference> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300001571> .
# 
# https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ColumnBase
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ColumnBase> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ColumnBase> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalElement> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ColumnBase> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Column Base"@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ColumnBase> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "The lower member on which a column shaft stands. Plinths and mouldings may be recorded as parts where survey resolution permits."@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ColumnBase> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/hasAATReference> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300233843> .
# 
# https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ColumnCapital
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ColumnCapital> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ColumnCapital> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalElement> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ColumnCapital> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Column Capital"@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ColumnCapital> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "The upper member of a column, at the transition from shaft to the element above. The capital may provide evidence for assigning a classical order."@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ColumnCapital> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/hasAATReference> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300001662> .
# 
# https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ColumnShaft
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ColumnShaft> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ColumnShaft> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalElement> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ColumnShaft> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Column Shaft"@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ColumnShaft> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "The main upright body of a column between its foot and capital. A shaft can consist of several drums while remaining one architectural element."@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ColumnShaft> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/hasAATReference> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300001754> .
# 
# https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ComponentID
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ComponentID> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ComponentID> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E42_Identifier> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ComponentID> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Component ID"@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ComponentID> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "An identifier assigned to distinguish a particular architectural entity within a survey, inventory or information system. The same component may carry identifiers from more than one scheme."@en .
# 
# https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ConstructionTechnique
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ConstructionTechnique> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ConstructionTechnique> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E55_Type> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ConstructionTechnique> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Construction Technique"@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ConstructionTechnique> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "A controlled concept denoting a method of assembling, shaping or applying building fabric. The same technique can classify work undertaken at different dates."@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ConstructionTechnique> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/hasAATReference> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300379526> .
# 
# https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ConstructionalLayer
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ConstructionalLayer> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ConstructionalLayer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E24_Physical_Human-Made_Thing> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ConstructionalLayer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Constructional Layer"@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ConstructionalLayer> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "A physically identifiable layer of an architectural element, distinguished by its material composition, constructional function, or position within a layered assembly. It may constitute a structural, protective, or finishing layer and can be identified as a distinct physical part regardless of whether it was formed through a single or multiple construction activities."@en .
# 
# https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Cornice
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Cornice> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Cornice> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalElement> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Cornice> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Cornice"@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Cornice> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "A projecting horizontal member that crowns an entablature or terminates a wall. The projection may also throw rainwater clear of the surface below."@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Cornice> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/hasAATReference> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300001788> .
# 
# https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/DiscreteBuildingUnit
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/DiscreteBuildingUnit> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/DiscreteBuildingUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E24_Physical_Human-Made_Thing> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/DiscreteBuildingUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Discrete Building Unit"@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/DiscreteBuildingUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "An individually distinguishable piece of building fabric used in construction or assembly. Its physical boundaries allow the same piece to be followed through reuse or displacement."@en .
# 
# https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Dome
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Dome> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Dome> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalElement> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Dome> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Dome"@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Dome> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "A curved covering rising above a space around a central area or axis. This class identifies the physical covering, including domes formed by several shells."@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Dome> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/hasAATReference> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300001280> .
# 
# https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/DomeType
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/DomeType> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/DomeType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E55_Type> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/DomeType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Dome Type"@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/DomeType> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "A controlled concept used to classify domes by form or construction. The classification can describe a shell arrangement independently of its material."@en .
# 
# https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Drawing
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Drawing> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Drawing> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E73_Information_Object> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Drawing> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Drawing"@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Drawing> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "This class comprises identifiable graphical information resources that represent architectural forms, spatial configurations, dimensions, construction details, or design concepts through lines, symbols, annotations, and other graphic conventions. It includes manually produced and computer-aided drawings, such as architectural plans, elevations, sections, measured survey drawings, technical drawings, and reconstruction drawings. Drawings may document existing or historical conditions, communicate design proposals, or express hypothetical interpretations of architectural structures. The class concerns the informational content of drawings, independently of their production technique, physical support, or digital format. Two-dimensional CAD drawings are included, whereas three-dimensional geometric models are represented separately."@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Drawing> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/hasAATReference> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300033973> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Drawing> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/hasAATReference> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300034395> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Drawing> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/hasAATReference> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300034787> .
# 
# https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/EngagedColumn
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/EngagedColumn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/EngagedColumn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalElement> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/EngagedColumn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Engaged Column"@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/EngagedColumn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "A column whose shaft projects from and is partly embedded in a wall or pier. Its exposed shaft retains the profile of a column."@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/EngagedColumn> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/hasAATReference> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300001638> .
# 
# https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Entablature
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Entablature> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Entablature> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalElement> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Entablature> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Entablature"@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Entablature> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "The horizontal superstructure of a classical order. Its architrave, frieze and cornice can be recorded individually even where they are cut from the same stone."@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Entablature> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/hasAATReference> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300001770> .
# 
# https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Facade
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Facade> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Facade> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalAssemblies> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Facade> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Facade"@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Facade> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "The exterior face of a building considered as a composed whole, including its openings, divisions and applied elements. Each elevation may be documented separately."@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Facade> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/hasAATReference> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300002526> .
# 
# https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/FinalRender
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/FinalRender> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/FinalRender> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ConstructionalLayer> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/FinalRender> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Final Render"@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/FinalRender> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "The outer finishing coat of a render system. The surface may be worked or coloured, while the coat remains identifiable by its position and material extent."@en .
# 
# https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Frieze
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Frieze> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Frieze> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalElement> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Frieze> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Frieze"@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Frieze> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "The middle division of an entablature, between architrave and cornice. Surface carving may be recorded as a decorative feature of the frieze."@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Frieze> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/hasAATReference> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300001816> .
# 
# https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/GeometricModel
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/GeometricModel> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/GeometricModel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E73_Information_Object> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/GeometricModel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Geometric Model"@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/GeometricModel> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "This class comprises identifiable digital information resources that represent the three-dimensional geometry of physical or conceptual objects through explicit or mathematically defined geometric structures. Such representations may include polygonal meshes, boundary representations, NURBS curves and surfaces, solid models, and parametric geometric models. Geometric models may describe surveyed architectural conditions, document historical configurations, support hypothetical reconstructions, or communicate design proposals. The class emphasizes geometric representation and does not require the explicit semantic classification of architectural components or the information structures characteristic of Building Information Modeling."@en .
# 
# https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Keystone
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Keystone> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Keystone> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/DiscreteBuildingUnit> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Keystone> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Keystone"@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Keystone> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "The crown unit closing an arch or a corresponding convergence of vault members. Record its position in the arch separately from any carving on its exposed face."@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Keystone> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/hasAATReference> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300001183> .
# 
# https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/LevellingCoat
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/LevellingCoat> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/LevellingCoat> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ConstructionalLayer> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/LevellingCoat> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Levelling Coat"@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/LevellingCoat> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "A preparatory coat applied to fill irregularities and establish a plane for a later finish. Its position beneath that finish helps identify it in an exposed section."@en .
# 
# https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/MasonryLayer
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/MasonryLayer> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/MasonryLayer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ConstructionalLayer> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/MasonryLayer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Masonry Layer"@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/MasonryLayer> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "A coherent thickness of masonry within a larger element, distinguished by its position or construction. A layer can include numerous stones or bricks and their joints."@en .
# 
# https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/MasonryUnit
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/MasonryUnit> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/MasonryUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/DiscreteBuildingUnit> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/MasonryUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Masonry Unit"@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/MasonryUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "An individual stone, brick or block laid as a constituent of masonry. A record identifies one unit even when many units share the same manufactured type."@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/MasonryUnit> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/hasAATReference> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300159910> .
# 
# https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/MasonryUnitType
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/MasonryUnitType> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/MasonryUnitType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E55_Type> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/MasonryUnitType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Masonry Unit Type"@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/MasonryUnitType> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "A controlled concept for classifying individual masonry units by form, manufacture or constructional use."@en .
# 
# https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Niche
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Niche> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Niche> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalElement> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Niche> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Niche"@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Niche> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "A recess formed in the face of a wall or another architectural element. Its back and sides define a distinct feature that may be recorded independently of any object displayed inside it."@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Niche> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/hasAATReference> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300002704> .
# 
# https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Pediment
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Pediment> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Pediment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/ArchitecturalElement> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Pediment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Pediment"@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Pediment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "A crowning element in the form of a gable above a portico, doorway or window. A pediment can be triangular, curved or broken. It includes the framing cornices and the field they enclose."@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Pediment> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/hasAATReference> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300002726> .
# 
# https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Photograph
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Photograph> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Photograph> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E73_Information_Object> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Photograph> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Photograph"@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Photograph> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "This class comprises identifiable information resources consisting of still photographic images produced through photographic processes, including analog and digital photography and the digitization of photographic originals. It includes historical photographs, contemporary survey photographs, detailed architectural photographs, and photographic documentation of construction and conservation activities. Photographs may depict existing architectural conditions, historical states, physical models, or proposed architectural designs. The class refers to photographic information content independently of its physical or digital carrier, file format, documentary function, or interpretation."@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Photograph> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/hasAATReference> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300046300> .
