# 
# https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Storey
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Storey> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Storey> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E53_Place> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Storey> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Storey"@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Storey> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "This class comprises identifiable spatial regions corresponding to the vertical organization of a building into distinct levels. Instances of this class represent spatial subdivisions of a building generally associated with a particular elevation or range of elevations.\n\nA storey may comprise one or more architectural spaces and may be associated with architectural elements located within or defining that level. Its spatial extent may be determined by the architectural configuration and vertical organization of the building.\n\nInstances of this class represent spatial regions rather than physical construction elements, and therefore should be distinguished from floor slabs, floor finishes, and other architectural elements forming the physical boundaries of a storey."@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Storey> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/hasAATReference> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300002667> .
# 
# https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Text
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Text> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Text> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E73_Information_Object> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Text> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Text"@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/Text> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "This class comprises identifiable information resources whose content is primarily expressed through written language. It includes historical records, archival documents, correspondence, scholarly publications, survey reports, conservation reports, descriptive accounts, and textual interpretations relating to architectural heritage. Textual resources may record actual conditions and historical events, present research findings, describe proposed interventions, or communicate hypothetical interpretations. The class concerns linguistic information content independently of its physical or digital carrier, publication status, file format, or documentary purpose. Textual content embedded in photographs, drawings, or other resources does not necessarily require the entire resource to be classified as Text."@en .
# 
# https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/TimberUnit
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/TimberUnit> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/TimberUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/DiscreteBuildingUnit> .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/TimberUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Timber Unit"@en .
<https://wanqin-liu.github.io/ahkto/TimberUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "One piece of worked timber incorporated into a construction. Joint lines and the continuity of the timber distinguish it from adjacent pieces."@en .
